## Consumption trace

GENHN-4 has only one weld dependency: the graded multiplication part of package field M3, supplied directly by W-9. It consumes no J-D0 clause.

| GENHN-4 display | Actual dependency | What is consumed |
|---|---|---|
| Recenter \(\Phi'\mapsto\Phi'+w\) | GENHN’s stage lift machinery | No M-field. This is an additive key recentering, not M4 representative covariance. |
| “Pass to \(\operatorname{gr}R=K^c[\mathbf Z/e_1\text{-graded lines}]\)” | W-9, hence the M3 field | Existence of the graded slots and their carry-twisted multiplication on the scored/exact-height layer. |
| “one \(K\)-slot per height; slot-min = valuation” | GENHN-2 | Not M1: no affine shear or harness/print valuation comparison is used. |
| \(\bar\Phi'\mapsto\bar\Phi'+\bar s\), giving \(R(T+s)\) | Formal polynomial substitution plus the M3 multiplication law | Only multiplication of exact-height slot representatives and its carry factors. |
| \(R(T)=(T-s)^\mu\), hence \(R(T+s)=T^\mu\) | Formal identity | No weld field and no characteristic assumption. |
| “twist powers … enter residual assembly and carry products identically” | The carry-cocycle portion of M3/W-9 | This is the sole substantive junction-note consumption. It does not use M2’s \(t/\varepsilon\) print-character transport. |
| Correction inequality \((i-j)\kappa+(\mu-i)\kappa+1=(\mu-j)\kappa+1\) | Native \(dv\)-multiplicativity and strict correction depth | No M1 or M3: these terms have already left the exact graded layer. |
| Overflow lands in-window and moves upward | GENHN-3(c),(d) | No M0. The reduction is GENHN’s own polynomial redivision, not a comparison of two division calculi. |
| Triangularity and injectivity | GENHN’s digit ordering | No weld or J-D0 input. |
| Onto “by cardinality” | GENHN-2 raw slot-string count | No J-D0 input. |
| \(|K|-1\) choices of \(s\) | Elementary residue-field count | No J-D0 input. |
| Invariant maintenance after adding \(\hat s\,n(\kappa)\) | Side-height inequality and GENHN’s key invariants | No M4 covariance theorem. |

Thus, field by field:

- M0: not consumed.
- M1: not consumed.
- M2: not consumed.
- M3: consumed only through W-9’s exact-height graded multiplication/carry law.
- M4: not consumed.

No cross-face coherence is used. WELD-M-PKG’s lack of such coherence is therefore harmless here.

GENHN-4 also does not consume WM-COB, WM-RHO, WM-CLASS, WM-FENCE, or any gauge-uniqueness assertion.

## J-D0 trace

Neither corrected J-D0 clause is load-bearing:

- J-D0(i), gauge invariance, does not apply. Its action is the multiplicative rescaling
  \[
  R(y)\longmapsto \xi^{-\deg R}R(\xi y),
  \]
  whereas GENHN refines by the additive translation
  \[
  R(T)\longmapsto R(T+s).
  \]
  J-D0’s own NONCHAR tooth confirms that an additive slot shift is outside its gauge theorem.

- J-D0(ii), value-blindness at fixed full count-shape \(\widehat T\), does not prove GENHN’s surjectivity count. GENHN compares a pinned refine slice with a floored node, not two realizations already known to have the same \((\Lambda_j,\mathcal G)\). Indeed \((T-s)^\mu\) and \(T^\mu\) may differ in nonzero-constant census data recorded by \(\Lambda_j\).

- J-D0’s \(\mu_{\widehat T}(q)\) is a normalized L3×L4 coefficient. GENHN needs literal finite digit-space cardinalities. GENHN-2 supplies those directly.

Therefore the J-D0 replacement map is simply: no edge existed; retain GENHN-2.

## T1 replacement of M3/W-9

The global W-9 frame can be replaced by a local graded-slot corollary of T1.C2.

For exact-height representatives, put
\[
\bar\tau_i(a,b)=
\operatorname{res}\!\left(
\frac{\widehat n_i(a)\widehat n_i(b)}
     {\widehat n_i(a+b)}
\right).
\]
T1.C2 gives
\[
[d]_a[d']_b=[dd'\bar\tau_i(a,b)]_{a+b},
\]
and C2-cocycle gives associativity. Repetition gives
\[
\widehat n_i(\kappa)^r
=
\widehat n_i(r\kappa)
\prod_{v=1}^{r-1}\tau_i(v\kappa,\kappa),
\]
whose residue is exactly the telescope/twist factor used in GENHN’s \(z^{fl_r}\) bookkeeping.

The remaining identifications route as follows:

| Former M3/W-9 use | T1 replacement |
|---|---|
| Twisted multiplication of graded slots | C2-cocycle plus the displayed local slot-product corollary |
| Powers \(n(\kappa)^r=z^{fl_r}n(r\kappa)\) | C2-vartheta and C2-recursion; C2-level-1 where applicable |
| Coherent digit versus multiplicative coefficient | C3-dictionary |
| Identical twist in residual assembly and carry products | C2 telescope together with C3-dictionary |
| Coefficient killing | The preceding local product law plus the formal identity \(R(T+s)=T^\mu\) |

C3-canonical-read may be cited if GENHN phrases its residual coefficient through that read, but the stronger global B-law or a theorem about all homogeneous initial forms is unnecessary. The GENHN products are the specific exact-height normalizer products handled by C2.

T1.C1, C4, C5, and C6 are not needed for the general refine-transfer argument. In particular, C6’s level-one domain \(M>D'h\) must not be mistaken for the general-stage existence of \(w\); that remains part of GENHN’s own stage-lift setup.

The revised dependency line is therefore
\[
\mathrm{GENHN\!-\!4}
\leftarrow
\{\mathrm{GENHN\!-\!2},\,
  \mathrm{GENHN\!-\!3(c,d)},\,
  \mathrm{T1.C2},\,
  \mathrm{T1.C3\text{-dictionary}},\,
  R(T+s)=T^\mu,\,
  \text{stage lift existence}\}.
\]
The direct edge
\[
\mathrm{GENHN\!-\!4}\leftarrow W\!-\!9\equiv M3
\]
can then be deleted.

## VERDICT: SG-2 VIABLE

The sole junction-note consumption is M3/W-9’s local exact-height carry multiplication, and T1.C2–C3 export precisely the smaller law GENHN-4 needs. M0, M1, M2, M4, and all of J-D0 are absent from the actual load-bearing trace.

This is a structural verdict, not yet a grade upgrade: revised T1 is still awaiting its hostile arc. Before the certified dependency graph is cut over, the local graded-slot corollary above should be stated explicitly and T1 accepted. No cross-face coherence theorem is required.
